model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "MCP session objects keep bearer and forwarded-grant revalidation on their own invocation database. Browser grants, discovery metadata and connection management use the existing API Worker's private service binding and its unchanged auth service. Replies encode and decode the original success and refusal schemas; transport and decode failures become AuthenticationUnavailable, with no fallback or cached authority. The MCP Worker carries neither an OAuth server nor the auth database adapter."
    }
  }
  extend basalt.build {
    metadata {
      constraint "The production MCP upload guard rejects OAuth-provider and auth-adapter modules as well as migration engines. Unused schema and route factories are pure initializers; retained factories keep their original expressions. Skill frontmatter imports only the YAML parser, with the same parser options and validation. Worker upload budgets stay unchanged."
    }
  }
}
